mentioned they prefer the message tool, but it seems that's not available. I could use the format MEDIA:url to send the image inline. So, I would need to structure my response with the first token as the reply tag, followed by the text and then the MEDIA link. That should work fine!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] Skin cancer pipeline ran on your image.\n\n**Skin Cancer Detector**\n- **Skin cancer class:** Benign nevus\n- **Confidence:** 0.9984\n- **Inference time:** 2.2316 s\n\n**Image Analyzer**\n- **Prediction:** nv\n- **CAM coverage:** 0.1202\n- **CAM center ratio:** 0.9231\n- **CAM left-right asymmetry:** 0.5915\n- **CAM top-bottom asymmetry:** 0.1353\n- **CAM explanation:** The model focused on features it described as asymmetry with central structural homogeneity.\n\n**X-AI summary**\n- The pipeline’s summary says this image was classified as a **benign nevus with high confidence**.\n- It also notes that this should still be correlated with a clinical skin exam and, if needed, dermoscopy or biopsy.\n\n**Recommended next steps from the pipeline**\n1. Dermatologic clinical evaluation\n2. Consider dermoscopy or other imaging\n3. Biopsy if uncertainty remains\n\nImportant: this is a **preliminary model signal, not a diagnosis**. If this spot is new, changing, asymmetric, bleeding, itchy, or otherwise concerning, it’s worth getting checked by a dermatologist.\n\nAnalyzer image:\nMEDIA:http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/admin/retrieve-image-file/nodes_bucket/626130f7c71f6b9e651c76be/69be3b4593ce5ab1f19b2cfb/f24835f7-b34e-4aea-8dd0-437ace0cbe99.jpg\n\nIf you want, I can also give you a **plain-English interpretation** of what these metrics likely mean.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0b0ca2a593440d770169cce59e083c819182dab99920ac2f3b\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":11015,"output":423,"cacheRead":12672,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":24110,"cost