{"type":"message","id":"caa47f3d","parentId":"8ad579ad","timestamp":"2026-04-01T11:35:03.690Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] Done — the pipeline ran on this new image too.\n\n**Skin Cancer Detector**\n- **Skin cancer class:** Benign nevus\n- **Confidence:** 0.9984\n- **Inference time:** 2.2895 s\n\n**Image Analyzer**\n- **Prediction:** nv\n- **CAM coverage:** 0.1199\n- **CAM center ratio:** 0.9229\n- **CAM left-right asymmetry:** 0.5957\n- **CAM top-bottom asymmetry:** 0.1383\n- **CAM explanation:** The model focused on patterns it described as asymmetry with central structural homogeneity.\n\n**X-AI summary**\n- The pipeline summary again labels this as a **benign nevus with high confidence**.\n- It recommends dermatologist review and correlation with the real clinical appearance.\n\n**Recommended next steps from the pipeline**\n1. Consult a dermatologist\n2. Review history such as sun exposure and family history\n3. Do a proper skin exam, with dermoscopy if needed\n\nImportant: this is still a **preliminary model output, not a diagnosis**. If the lesion is changing, irregular, bleeding, painful, or looks different from your other moles, get it checked in person.\n\nAnalyzer image:\nMEDIA:http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/admin/retrieve-image-file/nodes_bucket/626130f7c71f6b9e651c76be/69be3b4593ce5ab1f19b2cfb/b3792078-5fa7-4351-b17b-a2a5f71fbe59.jpg\n\nIf you want, I can also **compare the first and second pipeline results side by side**.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0b0ca2a593440d770169cd02e10b048191870a0c1c0252cc0e\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":11177,"output":364,"cacheRead":24064,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":35605,"cost":{"input":0.027942500000000002,"output":0.0054600000000000004,"cacheRead":0.006016,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0394185}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1775043295243}}
