{"type":"message","id":"84e88218","parentId":"0d40e78c","timestamp":"2026-04-01T11:45:23.986Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] Done — I ran the skin cancer pipeline on this image too.\n\n**Skin Cancer Detector**\n- **Skin cancer class:** Benign nevus\n- **Confidence:** 0.9984\n- **Inference time:** 2.5188 s\n\n**Image Analyzer**\n- **Prediction:** nv\n- **CAM coverage:** 0.1199\n- **CAM center ratio:** 0.9229\n- **CAM left-right asymmetry:** 0.5957\n- **CAM top-bottom asymmetry:** 0.1383\n- **CAM explanation:** The model focused on visual patterns it describes as asymmetry with central structural homogeneity.\n\n**X-AI summary**\n- The pipeline again classified the lesion as a **benign nevus with high confidence**.\n- It also says other possibilities should still be considered clinically, including atypical nevus or melanoma, and recommends proper medical review.\n\n**Recommended next steps from the pipeline**\n1. Review clinically rather than relying on the image alone\n2. Consider other possibilities if the spot is atypical\n3. Check medical history and do a full skin exam\n\nImportant: this remains a **preliminary model signal, not a diagnosis**. If this lesion is changing, irregular, bleeding, darker than your other moles, or worries you for any reason, an in-person dermatologist review is the right next step.\n\nAnalyzer image:\nMEDIA:http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/admin/retrieve-image-file/nodes_bucket/626130f7c71f6b9e651c76be/69be3b4593ce5ab1f19b2cfb/459e5e41-a6e5-400c-8c5c-178dd024c5d0.jpg\n\nIf you want, I can now **compare all three runs side by side** and tell you whether the outputs are consistent.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0b0ca2a593440d770169cd054caeb881918e3c08139b2b18ca\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":11185,"output":399,"cacheRead":35840,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":47424,"cost":{"i